{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:smooth-orientation","title":"def:smooth-orientation","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":1304,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#def:smooth-orientation","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"def:smooth-orientation","line":2228,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Smooth Orientation]\n\\label{def:smooth-orientation}\n\n\n\n\nA pointwise orientation of a smooth $n$-manifold $M$ assigns an orientation $o_x$ to each $T_xM$. It is \\emph{smooth} if every point has a neighbourhood carrying a smooth local frame positively oriented for $o_x$ at every point. An oriented Riemannian manifold is a Riemannian manifold with a smooth orientation.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Smooth Orientation] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a736d6f6f74682d6f7269656e746174696f6e\"></span> <p></p>A pointwise orientation of a smooth <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$n$\">$n$</span>-manifold <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> assigns an orientation <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$o_x$\">$o_x$</span> to each <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_xM$\">$T_xM$</span>. It is <em>smooth</em> if every point has a neighbourhood carrying a smooth local frame positively oriented for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$o_x$\">$o_x$</span> at every point. An oriented Riemannian manifold is a Riemannian manifold with a smooth orientation. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:inner-products-of-tensors","next":"re